(Title) Tj
T*
(Prevention of Heel Tissue Breakdown in High-Risk Patients: Protocol for a Multi-Site) Tj
T*
(Implementation Trial) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Rationale: Pressure-related tissue damage at the heel remains a significant complication) Tj
T*
(in acute care settings, yet the optimal timing and approach for prevention across) Tj
T*
(different care phases has not been systematically studied. Protocol: This multi-site) Tj
T*
(randomized trial will evaluate whether prophylactic use of a specialized heel protection) Tj
T*
(device reduces the incidence of heel tissue injury in 180 hospitalized patients with) Tj
T*
(neurological conditions or significantly limited mobility. Participants will be enrolled) Tj
T*
(upon arrival at participating ambulance services and followed continuously through) Tj
T*
(emergency departments and hospital ward stays at two academic medical centers in Sweden.) Tj
T*
(Those assigned to the intervention group will receive the protective device applied in the) Tj
T*
(pre-hospital setting and maintained throughout hospitalization; the control group will) Tj
T*
(receive standard positioning and repositioning protocols. Primary outcomes will assess) Tj
T*
(tissue integrity at multiple time-points across the care pathway. Secondary aims will) Tj
T*
(evaluate the feasibility of early implementation in prehospital settings and identify) Tj
T*
(clinical or demographic predictors of tissue breakdown. Risk stratification using) Tj
T*
(validated assessment tools will be performed at each care transition.) Tj
ET
